  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Location correction: contrary to what our previous fiche stated, Beau Rivage is not on the Promenade des Anglais but at 107 quai des États-Unis, on the Vieux Nice side (confirmed by 2 consistent sources, including the official site plagenicebeaurivage.com). It's a private beach, bar and restaurant all in one, with a direct view over the Baie des Anges, seating up to 550 guests (1,200 for cocktail-style events).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The establishment is one of the addresses carrying the official "Pet Friendly" label awarded by the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office since 2022 — an audited scheme, not just a box ticked in a directory. Two independent sources confirm dogs are welcome: the official tourist office page and a specialised directory (no size limit mentioned). Hours: breakfast from 9am, lunch 12pm-3:30pm, dinner 7pm-10pm from May to September (continuous service 12pm-10:30pm at the height of summer).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ask for a table on the beach side — your dog will appreciate the direct access to the sand and water.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Promenade des Anglais is perfect for a long walk before or after the meal, and Vieux Nice is about fifteen minutes on foot.</p>
